      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The doctrine of unconscionability ... is a general, state, common-law, contract-law principle that is not specific to arbitration, and does not implicate the FAA.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012)"
    },
    {
      "kind": "kinetic",
